{
  "id": "f06",
  "rule": "the themes routes (/wp/v2/themes and /wp/v2/themes/<stylesheet>, Part G v01-v07) on WordPress with the harness theme quarkpress active, compared field by field with QuarkPress's synthetic theme: the active theme for an editor, an author and a contributor, with and without the editor's context=edit (identical bodies, X-WP-Total 1, Allow GET); a subscriber (403) and anonymous (401) refused the active theme; bob's other lists refused (403 rest_cannot_view_themes, no Allow) and status[]=active accepted; status=foo refused before permission (400, no Allow) for bob and anonymous; alice's full and inactive lists (D54: WordPress lists every installed theme); the active theme's item for bob, erin and anonymous, another theme's and an unknown one for bob (403) and alice (404 rest_theme_not_found with Allow; D54 for the installed one); a percent-encoded stylesheet decoded once (also a doubly encoded one, decoded by the request path and then by the route); nested _fields; HEAD; OPTIONS of both routes",
  "setup": [
    {
      "option": "qp_parity_quarkpress_theme",
      "value": "1"
    }
  ],
  "requests": [
